  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1215 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nStarting the extended period Tuesday, high pressure is forecast to \ncontinue to slightly extend northward across the area. The further \nnorth the high pressure can go then the warmer temperatures will be. \nCurrent forecast has temperatures returning to the mid to upper\n90s, but if the high pressure can remain a little further south\nthen highs in the upper 80s to low 90s would be common. The \nposition of high will also dictate precipation chances as well.\nWith the current forecast being on the warmer end this does \ndecrease our precipitation chances as guidance indicates that a\nshortwave will develop on the northern periphery of the high. \nIf storms were to develop, they would turn severe with damaging \nwinds the main threat as they form a cluster and move to the \nsoutheast. Currently should storms develop the northern and \neastern portions of the area would be favored. \n\nWednesday, has a similar pattern but is more dictate by the \ndevelopment of a ridge across the western CONUS. Again guidance \nindicates another shortwave within the flow which could move into \nthe area and possibly entire most if not the entire forecast area. \nCurrent guidance indicates that shear is a little better around\n35- 40 knots which could support a damaging wind and perhaps \neven large hail threat if storms don't grow upscale too quickly.\nThose two days will need to be continued to be monitored. \n\nThursday, through the end of the forecast period indicates that \nanother strong ridge will develop across the western CONUS as warm \ntemperatures in the low to mid 90s return. The amplitude of the\nridge will dictate how warm it gets and if precipitation \nchances occur as we may continue to reside on the eastern side \nof said ridge.",
